@reactions tradition
// Writer-commons, reactions batch 2. The day after a tradition (social's cue tradition.<id>, one day): what people
// say about it, and (.you) to someone who came. Said the next day, so it's past tense.

? cue:tradition.quiz !cue:tradition.quiz.you
- Did you hear about quiz night? Two teams tied on the reactor question. Again.   #funny
- Missed you at the quiz. We could've used someone who knows engines.
? cue:tradition.quiz.you tier>=acquaintance
- Good team last night. You got the one about the coils. I'd never have got that.
- Quiz night was brilliant. We were robbed on the reactor question, though.   #funny
? cue:tradition.quiz.you tier>=friend
- Same team next week? Don't say no. I've already told everyone.   #warm

? cue:tradition.film !cue:tradition.film.you
- Film night was a good one. Someone cried. Nobody's saying who.   #funny
? cue:tradition.film.you tier>=acquaintance
- Did you like the film? I liked the bit with the lighthouse.
- You laughed at the right bits last night. Not everyone does.   #warm

? cue:tradition.jam !cue:tradition.jam.you
- The jam went late. Someone played the same song three times. Different words each time.   #funny
? cue:tradition.jam.you tier>=acquaintance
- Saw you at the jam. Did you sing? I think you sang. I'm counting it.   #funny
- Good jam last night. The guitars were nearly in tune.

? cue:tradition.observatory-night !cue:tradition.observatory-night.you
- Clear sky at observatory night. Four little telescopes and the big one.
? cue:tradition.observatory-night.you tier>=acquaintance
- I saw a star go out last night. No, wait. It was a smudge on the window.   #funny
- Good to see you up at the observatory. It's better with more people.   #warm

? cue:tradition.running !cue:tradition.running.you
- Gym club went well. Nobody fell off the treadmill. A record.   #funny
? cue:tradition.running.you tier>=acquaintance
- You came running! Your legs will hate you by lunch. That's how you know it worked.   #funny

? cue:tradition.market !cue:tradition.market.you
- Swap meet was busy. Someone swapped a jumper for a cactus. Called Gerald, obviously.   #funny
? cue:tradition.market.you tier>=acquaintance
- Did you find anything good at the swap meet? I got a book with all the pages. Rare.

? cue:tradition.harvest !cue:tradition.harvest.you
- Harvest morning! Fresh salad with dinner tonight. Real tomatoes.
- The garden picked a whole crate of beans. Brennan's thrilled. She hummed.   #funny
? cue:tradition.harvest dept:galley
- The harvest's in. Beans, roots, tomatoes. Dinner writes itself tonight.
? cue:tradition.harvest dept:garden
- Good harvest. Week fourteen tomatoes. Best age for a tomato.
? cue:tradition.harvest.you tier>=acquaintance
- You helped with the harvest! Your hands smell of tomato leaves. The good smell.   #warm
? cue:tradition.harvest.you dept:garden
- {thanks} for the help this morning. You pick gently. Not everyone does.   #warm

? cue:tradition.birthday !cue:tradition.birthday.you
- There was birthday cake in the mess last night. I had two slices.   #funny
- Did you get any of the birthday cake? It went in about a minute.
? cue:tradition.birthday dept:galley
- Birthday cake went down well. We sang. Badly. That's tradition.
? cue:tradition.birthday.you tier>=acquaintance
- Good of you to come for the cake last night. Everyone notices who comes.   #warm

? cue:tradition.hull-lights
- The hull lights looked lovely last night. The whole ship glowing.
? cue:tradition.founding
- Founding Day. The Wren's older than all of us, and still flying.   #warm

// Writer 4, batch 9: more harvest.
? cue:tradition.harvest !cue:tradition.harvest.you
- Harvest's in. The mess smells like a market.
- Baskets everywhere. Somebody grew a very big marrow.   #funny
? cue:tradition.harvest.you tier>=acquaintance
- You picked beans yesterday? {thanks}. They're in tonight's stew.
? cue:tradition.harvest.you tier>=friend
- Saw you with a basket. Come back next year. Bring a friend.   #warm
? cue:tradition.harvest.you dept:galley
- Your tomatoes are in the soup. Well, the garden's. You picked them.
? cue:tradition.harvest.you dept:garden
- Mm. You came to the harvest. Good hands. Gentle with the roots.   #warm
